{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789855-lunar-shapeshifting-and-merits","id":789855,"title":"Lunar Shapeshifting and Merits","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-20T12:07:03-08:00","id":789855,"title":"Lunar Shapeshifting and Merits","content":"Obviously, when a Lunar wears a stolen form, he loses any Supernatural Merits attached to his own form and gains the Supernatural Merits of the stolen form for as long as he wears it.*<br /> <br /> But looking at the Merits, I started to find questions with less obvious answers.<br /> <br /> <br /> Innate Standard Merits, for example, apparently need to be judged on a case-by-case basis instead of a blanket rule. Some seem appropriate for taking into other forms, others seem obviously inappropriate, and a few are ambiguous.<br /> <br /> Let us begin with the easiest one of all: <i>Giant</i>. No Lunar with the Giant Merit would enjoy it while wearing the form of someone who didn't have it. But the flipside of that coin is that even a Lunar without this Merit would get to enjoy it when wearing the form of someone who <i>did!</i><br /> <br /> The <i>Ambidexterity </i>Merit represents a natural talent rather than a trained skill, as it is not a Purchasable Merit. A Lunar who naturally has this Merit would thus seem incapable of enjoying it when wearing the form of someone who did <i>not </i>have it. But again, even a Lunar without this Merit would get to enjoy it when wearing the form of someone who <i>did.</i><br /> <br /> <i>Danger Sense</i>, <i>Direction Sense</i>, and <i>Eidetic Memory</i> are likewise brain-meat talents rather than trained skills, but Lunars already retain their Mental Attribute ratings regardless of their form, and these things are different from the Supernatural <i>Enhanced Sense</i> Merit. I would rule that a Lunar who has these Merits would enjoy them regardless of form, AND that a Lunar without any of these Merits would get to enjoy them when wearing the form of someone who <i>did </i>have them.<br /> <br /> <i>Hideous </i>is the first truly ambiguous Innate Merit. Whether it carries over across forms depends entirely on whether the condition is caused by injuries (scars, and.or broken bones that set improperly) and how Heart's Blood shapeshifting interacts with crippling injuries. (Such as what happens when a Lunar in griffin form loses one of his wings or forepaws and returns to a form with just four limbs. An octopus wouldn't consider losing a limb crippling because they regenerate tentacles, but legs and wings generally don't grow back.)<br /> <br /> <i>Natural Immunity</i> and <i>Selective Conception</i> are explicitly either entirely natural talents or perhaps the blessings of supernatural beings. Selective Conception further claims that it can be the result of training and deliberate skill, but this is belied by the Merit's classification as Innate rather than Purchased. I would err on the side of &quot;totally dependent on the form&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <i>Purchased </i>Standard Merits are trickier. For the most part, they appear to be learned skills (Quickdraw), but others are conditions trained into the body as naturally as another dot of Strength (such as Strong Lungs or Poison Resistance).<br /> <br /> Still, I could feel comfortable with ruling that the Lunar gets none of these Merits from stolen forms in return for getting to carry over these Merits from his own true form. Also, the Lunar could use an Intelligence Charm to tap into the memories and skills of his stolen Heart's Blood to treat the victim as a mentor for learning these skills for himself.<br /> <br /> <br /> I think it should be thoroughly appropriate that a Lunar NEVER gets to &quot;double-stack&quot; the benefits of any single Merit if he happens to wear a form that has it while also having it in his birth shape. His Danger Sense never becomes more acute and his Poison Resistance never becomes hardier.<br /> <br /> <br /> As to Standard Merits and what Merits are or are not appropriate for building a werebeast War Form with Deadly Beastman Transformation...<br /> <br /> In Second Edition, the Large mutation was explicitly forbidden, but the Giant Merit is completely different. It's far more expensive, and the ONLY benefit it grants is a single additional -0 Health Level, without anything to do with your Attribute dots. Therefore, I think it's entirely appropriate for Third Edition War Forms, especially for Lunars born small but reborn with Elephant Totems.<br /> <br /> Hideous also seems appropriate, for players who want to play otherwise beautiful characters whose War Form reveals the dangerously ugly side of the character, or perhaps represents the character's desire to be horrifically intimidating in a way they could never have been in their original, mortal life.<br /> <br /> Natural Immunity and Danger Sense are perfectly appropriate, and Ambidexterity makes for a sensible complement to the Extra Limbs Supernatural Merit.<br /> <br /> But Eidetic Memory and Selective Conception seem thoroughly inappropriate to the <i>War</i> Form. If a Lunar was going to get either of these things, they seem more appropriate to his birth shape.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Finally, the exception to the rule at the very beginning:<br /> <br /> If a Lunar player chooses a Tell that can be mechanically represented with a Supernatural Merit, such as horns or a tail, I would rule that the Merit follows them across all forms precisely because it is the character's Tell.<br /> <br /> The Merit would need to be purchased at character generation with bonus points, or else with experience points if the character Exalts during play.<br /> <br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 12-20-2015, 05:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T13:43:18-08:00","id":789904,"title":"","content":"I think I get what you're saying - and I like it<br /> <br /> I guess its a drawback from the new merits system - telling merits that are a function of how you think (like eidetic memory) apart from merits that represent things you have learned makes sense - but ya... I can only imagine the kind of arguments and rules-lawyering it'll result in.<br /> <br /> Still, I like what you're presenting","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malfeas F'Tagn - go check out my epic MLP/Exalted crossover &quot;The Scroll of Exalted ponies&quot; @ Fimfiction","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/588-webkilla","name":"webkilla","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar588_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-20T14:46:34-08:00","id":789931,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>webkilla</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789855-lunar-shapeshifting-and-merits?p=789904#post789904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess its a drawback from the new merits system - telling merits that are a function of how you think (like eidetic memory) apart from merits that represent things you have learned makes sense</div> </div> </div> </div>I think the Innate and Purchased classifications are clear enough; you can easily and simply rule that:<br /> <br /> * Lunars only have <i>mental </i>Innate Merits and any Purchasable Merits carry over across all forms<br /> <br /> * none of the Lunar's <i>physical </i>Innate Merits carry over (without a Charm to allow it; probably one that lets the Lunar use his own physical Attributes when those are superior to the form's), but the Lunar enjoys any of the physical Innate Merits of the form he wears<br /> <br /> * enjoying the <i>mental </i>Innate Merits of the form he wears would probably be a function of a Charm that lets him borrow the victim's Social and Mental Attribute ratings, when those are superior to his own.<br /> <br /> * the Lunar never gets any of the victim's Purchasable Merits along with the stolen form, though a certain Intelligence Charm could help him learn those faster","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T15:07:52-07:00","id":892045,"title":"","content":"Should a Lunar need to spend Exp on the Latent abilities of animal forms they've taken? They are defined as such:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While an animal might be physically capable of performing these, it has no instinctive drive to do so, and thus requires training to use them. </div> </div> </div>These abilities are not matters of skill, but comprehension. The animal needs training to comprehend performing such actions and appreciating why they would want to perform such actions.<br /> <br /> As human beings, Lunar Exalted need no such enlightenment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T16:00:08-07:00","id":892083,"title":"","content":"And that's why new hires at McDonald's don't need to be taught <i>anything </i>in order to do their jobs. After all, they're human beings - that apparently changes whether possessing the physiology required to physically undertake an action includes the instinctive drive to do so. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-16-2016, 07:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T17:56:57-07:00","id":892151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789855-lunar-shapeshifting-and-merits?p=892045#post892045\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Should a Lunar need to spend Exp on the Latent abilities of animal forms they've taken? They are defined as such:</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Magical ones, too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As to Standard Merits and what Merits are or are not appropriate for building a werebeast War Form with Deadly Beastman Transformation... </div> </div> </div>I'd only use Hideous, which reflects the hybrid form being scary and threatening. Everything else can be covered in the effects of the Charm, as effects of a Charm instead of as Merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T18:29:17-07:00","id":892177,"title":"","content":"<i>Should</i> Lunars be able to use the magical abilities? They have Charms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T18:42:48-07:00","id":892181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/789855-lunar-shapeshifting-and-merits?p=892177#post892177\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>Should</i> Lunars be able to use the magical abilities? They have Charms.</div> </div> </div> </div>They have both. It's a perk of being a magical shapeshifter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}